 "title": "Fungal Response to Environmental Stressors and Chemicals",
 "summary": "This cluster involves various fungal organisms, including Candida albicans, Malassezia pachydermatis, and Scedosporium/Lomentospora, which respond to environmental stressors and chemicals. CO2 acts on C. albicans and germinates Scedosporium/Lomentospora. Candida glabrata undergoes morphological changes in response to CO2. Ketoconazole induces transcriptional responses in ERG11, ERG24, ERG25, ERG3, and ERG5. Malassezia pachydermatis induces stress in ketoconazole, and ribosome biogenesis is involved in the transcriptional response to Malassezia pachydermatis. ERG3 interacts with several genes and is upregulated by KTZ. KTZ is upregulated by ERG6 and M. pachydermatis is added to KTZ.",
